course: dictionary
lesson: 12004
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they leave clues.
explain: «We played checkers after tea.» Checkers here is a board game for two players. The clues are played and after tea, and a game fits both.
explain: «Mum counted the red checkers before we put them back in the box.» Now checkers means the round flat pieces. Counting and putting them in a box only makes sense for pieces.
explain: «The checker at the till scanned our shopping quickly.» Here a checker is a person who checks things. Try the meaning in the sentence: a game would not scan shopping, but a person can.
fact: Checkers is a board game for two players.
fact: Players move round flat pieces diagonally on a squared board, and they can jump over the other player's pieces to capture them.
fact: The board has 64 squares, 8 by 8.
fact: A checker can also be a round piece used in the game, or a person who checks things, like at a supermarket.
fact: Checkers is used with a singular verb: «Checkers is my favourite game.» Playing checkers helps you plan and think ahead.
exercise: «We played checkers after tea.» What is checkers in this sentence? | *A board game for two players | A bus that goes to school | A squared map of the town | A kind of cake
exercise: How many squares does a checkers board have? | *64 | 36 | 16 | 100
exercise: «The checker at the till scanned our shopping quickly.» What does checker mean here? | A kind of bag for carrying shopping | A shop that sells food | A round piece used in a game | *A person who checks things
test: In checkers, how do the pieces move? | Round and round the edge of the board | They never move at all | *Diagonally, across the squares | Straight forward and backward, like a car
test: «Mum counted the red checkers before we put them back in the box.» What are checkers in this sentence? | A board with 100 squares | A person who counts things | *The round flat pieces used in the game | A game for two players
exam: Which meaning of checkers fits this sentence best: «Dad lost three games of checkers in a row»? | *A board game for two players | A person who checks things | A squared floor tile | A round piece on the shelf
